'''Monksthorpe''' is a [[hamlet (place)|hamlet]] in the [[Non-metropolitan district|district]] of [[East Lindsey]], [[Lincolnshire]], England. It lies {{convert|3|mi|km|0}} east from the town of [[Spilsby]] and north from the village of [[Great Steeping]] .
[[File:Monksthorpe Baptistry - geograph.org.uk - 1263231.jpg|thumb|140px|left|upright|Monksthorpe Baptistry]]

Monksthorpe chapel is a Grade II* [[listed building]] dating from 1701,<ref>{{NHLE|num=1223592|desc=Monksthorpe Baptist Chapel|accessdate=1 August 2011}}</ref>  now in the care of the [[National Trust for Places of Historic Interest or Natural Beauty|National Trust]]. In the grounds is a Grade II* listed open air total submersion [[Baptismal font|font]],<ref>{{NHLE|num=1267243|desc=Open air total submersion font|fewer-links=x|accessdate=1 August 2011}}</ref>  believed to be one of only two in the country.<ref>{{cite web|author=Judson, Paula|title=Monksthorpe Baptist Chapel|url=http://www.lincsheritage.org/community_heritage/guides_information/treasure_trove/article.php?id=21|work=Heritage Lincolnshire|publisher=The Heritage Trust of Lincolnshire|accessdate=1 August 2011|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111001234438/http://www.lincsheritage.org/community_heritage/guides_information/treasure_trove/article.php?id=21|archive-date=1 October 2011|url-status=dead}}</ref>
